  "body": "Since the search engines consider the form pre-filled data as a volatile data, is it possible to add an attribute to declare when the data isn't volatile?\r\n\r\nIt can be usefull to decorate (in CSS) a form as a simple view (visually not as a form), to reduce the need to create 2 view, one to read, one to edit... then reduce also the need to make a call to the server to edit the data, but preverse the data relevance for the search engines.\r\n\r\nExample: http://lcfvs.github.io/form.cheats.editable/\r\n\r\n(Please consider I'm not a designer, the following demos can hurt your eyes, but the real insterest resides in its CSS mechanic.)",
